<title>USA: AARP picks three health insurers, drops Prudential.</title>
<headline>AARP picks three health insurers, drops Prudential.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The American Association of Retired Persons said it has selected three insurers to provide its members with health insurance products, ending its contract, valued at $4.5 billion annually in premiums, with Prudential Insurance Co of America.</p>
<p>AARP said it selected United Healthcare Corp to provide Medicare supplement and hospital indemnity insurance; Metropolitan Life Insurance Co to provide long-term care insurance and ITT Hartford Group Inc to provide customer service for all health insurance products.</p>
</text>
